    <h3>Key Functionalities:</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Adaptive multi-domain technical interviews across Written, Coding, and SQL domains</li>
        <li>17-node LangGraph interview orchestration with dynamic routing and context-aware navigation</li>
        <li>Hybrid RAG + LLM question generation with semantic deduplication</li>
        <li>Conversational Humanizer with deterministic selection and follow-up validation</li>
        <li>Policy-driven contextual follow-up engine with guard validation</li>
        <li>Dimensional answer evaluation across technical depth, system design, engineering judgment, communication, and behavioral signals</li>
        <li>Deterministic Interview Reasoner with 13 pattern detectors and no LLM dependency</li>
        <li>EvaluationSignalWriter mapping evaluation results to typed evidence signals</li>
        <li>Hire-decision gating with normalized scoring and explainability anchors</li>
        <li>LongitudinalProfile for cross-session candidate progress tracking</li>
        <li>Deterministic session replay graph and Replay UI with no LLM on the replay path</li>
        <li>Unified coaching report with executive summary, strengths, knowledge gaps, strategy, and benchmark</li>
        <li>PDF and JSON report export</li>
        <li>Business context integration using job descriptions and company descriptions</li>
        <li>Chroma vector corpus with Hugging Face Dataset backup and restore</li>
        <li>Feature-flagged experimental paths for humanizer, follow-up, and adaptive navigation</li>
        <li>Production-oriented QA harness covering backend, UI, and stress verification</li>
        <li>Strict Domain-Driven Design architecture with frozen contracts and inward-only dependencies</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Adaptive Interview Setup</h3>
    <p>
        The interview starts from a configurable setup where the candidate can select the interview type, seniority
        level, interview length, and preferred coding languages. This initial configuration establishes the scope and
        difficulty of the session and provides the foundation for the adaptive interview flow across Written, Coding,
        and SQL domains.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/57ff54b1-72ec-416d-8398-f6a363a86d8e"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="AI Interview Simulator Setup" />

    <h3>Business Context &amp; Advanced Interview Configuration</h3>
    <p>
        Optional company and role context can be added to tailor the interview experience and generated questions.
        The platform uses this session-level business context together with seniority and interview configuration
        to adapt question generation, coverage management, and navigation to different technical profiles and
        business scenarios.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7c7a2951-45b3-41ea-92ec-607c97c87cf1"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Advanced Interview Context Setup" />

    <h3>Adaptive Technical Interview Flow</h3>
    <p>
        Questions are generated and selected through a hybrid RAG + LLM pipeline and organized across multiple
        technical domains. The interview graph maintains session coverage and candidate context while dynamically
        routing the conversation. Written questions can explore problem-solving, technical background, and
        engineering experience, with the next question influenced by the candidate's previous responses.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4b9dcc93-d62e-4788-b6c1-5a30aff27b98"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Technical Background Question" />

    <h3>Structured Answer Evaluation &amp; Coaching</h3>
    <p>
        Every submitted answer is evaluated through a structured pipeline that produces a score, strengths,
        improvement areas, and actionable suggestions. The evaluation is designed to provide useful coaching rather
        than a simple pass/fail result, while the resulting signals can feed subsequent reasoning and the final
        interview assessment.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/38d6e092-a74e-4a91-bfab-b05e7c94be6e"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Written Question Feedback" />

    <h3>Contextual Follow-Up &amp; Conversational Continuity</h3>
    <p>
        The follow-up engine generates policy-driven questions based on the candidate's previous answer and the
        current interview context. Follow-ups are LLM-generated but validated by deterministic guards, allowing
        the interview to behave more like a real technical conversation while preserving explicit control over
        coverage and question quality.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ba73cd4-c7f7-4a0f-9ada-7540e24a0984"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Contextual Technical Follow-Up" />

    <h3>Diagnostic Feedback &amp; Iterative Improvement</h3>
    <p>
        The platform distinguishes between correct, partial, and incorrect answers and provides targeted feedback
        for each case. For partial answers, the evaluation identifies what was correct, what is missing, and how
        the candidate could improve the response, with the option to retry before continuing the interview.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/22b674ae-8fd8-4e07-8634-5d12f1e8f565"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Partial Answer Feedback" />

    <h3>Interactive SQL Interview &amp; Automated Evaluation</h3>
    <p>
        The SQL domain provides database schemas, realistic data-access tasks, and an interactive query editor.
        Submitted queries are executed against test cases and evaluated automatically, producing structured results,
        scores, diagnostics, and improvement suggestions. This allows database knowledge to be assessed through
        executable evidence rather than purely theoretical questions.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7acd3d07-dd79-4d26-8c20-8a5f23921f11"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="SQL Database Question" />
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/66d741c6-6776-40ce-a78b-084371a1bc42"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="SQL Database Feedback" />

    <h3>AI-Assisted Debugging &amp; Hints</h3>
    <p>
        When a SQL solution fails, the simulator exposes test failures and diagnostic information and can provide
        an actionable AI-generated hint. The objective is not simply to mark the answer as wrong, but to guide the
        candidate toward identifying the underlying issue and improving the solution.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d685b2a7-8efd-40db-a4e3-32e2f29cc507" 
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="SQL Question Feedback with Hints" />

    <h3>Interactive Coding Challenges</h3>
    <p>
        Coding interviews provide a complete problem specification, execution contract, examples, and an interactive
        code editor. Solutions are evaluated against visible and hidden test cases, enabling the platform to assess
        implementation correctness and edge-case handling in a way that resembles a real technical coding assessment.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d125709f-6d4f-42ba-b21c-3806d06f5b4c"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Coding Interview Question" />

    <h3>Unified Interview Report</h3>
    <p>
        The final report is the sole scoring artifact and consolidates the interview outcome into a structured
        assessment. It includes an overall readiness score, executive summary, strengths, areas for improvement,
        and evidence-backed coaching insights. The report is designed to provide both a concise hiring signal and
        actionable guidance for the candidate.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f397941b-6445-4a06-bda7-157e9500e131"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Final Interview Report" />

    <h3>Knowledge Gaps &amp; Next Interview Strategy</h3>
    <p>
        The report translates interview evidence into prioritized development areas. Knowledge gaps are connected
        to the evaluated dimensions and converted into a next-interview strategy, giving the candidate concrete
        priorities for improving technical depth, system design, or other identified weaknesses.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c16145a4-ec37-457c-95c9-c2e62daf5f13"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Knowledge Gaps and Next Interview Strategy" />

    <h3>Dimension Analysis &amp; Question-Level Assessment</h3>
    <p>
        Performance is analyzed both at dimension level and at individual-question level. Dimension scores provide
        a high-level view of technical depth, system design, and problem solving, while question-level evidence
        exposes the specific strengths and weaknesses that contributed to the overall assessment.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e6160cea-0395-4c6b-879c-ab41f49ed42c"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Dimension Analysis and Question-Level Assessment" />

    <h3>Benchmarking, Decision Rationale &amp; Behavioral Insights</h3>
    <p>
        The reporting layer compares interview performance against a benchmark population and exposes the factors
        that influenced the readiness decision. Behavioral and narrative insights provide additional evidence about
        problem-solving patterns, system-level thinking, and other recurring signals observed during the interview.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19c3abf2-562f-4a42-a5b5-538485cc1052"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Interview Benchmark and Decision Rationale" />

    <h3>Progress Tracking &amp; Session History</h3>
    <p>
        After completing an interview, candidates can review their progress, download the generated report, replay
        a completed session, or start a new interview. The post-interview area also provides access to previous
        completed sessions and actions for continuing the interview workflow.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/22267ecc-f99a-427c-aa7c-6766674d65dd"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Progress Tracking and Session Actions" />

    <h3>Longitudinal Candidate Continuity</h3>
    <p>
        The platform preserves session history and supports longitudinal candidate development. This creates the
        foundation for comparing performance over time and using previous interview evidence to improve future
        preparation and assessment.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f4ab9ff1-c73c-4922-8548-e90b54b433e4"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="Session History and Progress Tracking" />

    <h3>Professional PDF Reporting</h3>
    <p>
        Interview results can be exported as a clean, printable PDF suitable for professional review. The generated
        document includes the overall score, executive summary, performance by dimension, benchmark information,
        and decision context, supporting both candidate coaching and structured evaluation workflows.
    </p>
    <img src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0d17f0af-807e-4cf1-b8ac-36c40cc290e7"
        class="portfolio-details__img" alt="PDF Interview Evaluation Report" />

